==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|κιρρός||tawny}} and {{m|en|-osis}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/sɪˈɹoʊsɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cirrhoses}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A chronic disease of the [[liver]] caused by damage from [[toxin]]s (including [[alcohol]]), metabolic problems, [[hepatitis]] or nutritional deprivation. It is characterised by an increase of fibrous tissue and the destruction of liver cells.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Interstitial inflammation of kidneys, lungs, and other organs.
#* {{RQ:Chmbrs YngrSt|VI}}
#*: “I don't mean all of your friends—only a small proportion—which, however, connects your circle with that deadly, idle, brainless bunch—the insolent chatterers at the opera,{{...}}the speed-mad fugitives from the furies of ennui, the neurotic victims of mental '''cirrhosis''', the jewelled animals whose moral code is the code of the barnyard—!”

